# The annotations of a generic declaration are made at each of its instances (§3.16), so the types
# their values are built of are held to what any type it holds is (§3.5, §3.17): a type match
# naming no type at an instance is reported where the instance is written, a field's, a variant
# field's and a function's alike, and an annotation naming its type again with a type argument
# built from its own makes it endless, as its field would.

